l-state and bounded failover evidence. Separately, the provider-wide restart protocol is complete on all four nodes: every node has a healthy pre-restart state, explicit restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, and cluster state. The command-level pre/post boot IDs exactly match the fixed baseline and after-executor boot observations.","limitations":["Failover was tested through brief, sequential single-Prometheus outages; the evidence does not measure sustained outage behavior, simultaneous failures, or performance under load, none of which was expressly required.","Historical persistence was probed at one timestamp and returned one matching stored series for each unavailable replica; it does not establish a long-term retention horizon.","Secret values were appropriately redacted, so final credential correctness is corroborated by their creation path and successful authenticated operations rather than literal value inspection.","The lifecycle collector does not inventory persistent application-data directories; retained boot-marker files are inferred from their writes, later reads, and the absence of cleanup in the complete command timeline."]}
